<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37519" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedictĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		2. praedico. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A premising</i>, in rhet., <i><span class="en">Quint. 9,
				2, 17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A foretelling</i>, <i>prediction.</i>—In sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedictio mali,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 25, 54</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">2, 42, 87</span></i> sq. —In
			plur.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 1, 2, 4</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. N. D. 2, 3, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 14</span></i>.</div>
